---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import { SITE, formatSiteAddress } from '../config/site';

const telHref = `tel:${(SITE.phoneDisplay ?? SITE.phone).replace(/\D/g, '')}`;
const address = formatSiteAddress();
---

<BaseLayout
  title={`Terms of Service | ${SITE.name}`}
  description={SITE.termsDescription}
>
  <Header />
  <main class="section legal-page">
    <div class="container legal-content panel-card">
      <p class="section-label">Legal</p>
      <h1>Terms of Service</h1>
      <p class="legal-updated">Last updated: July 22, 2026</p>
      <p>
        Welcome to <strong>{SITE.name}</strong>. By accessing this website or submitting a service
        or contact form, you agree to these Terms of Service. If you do not agree,
        please do not use the site. These terms mirror typical home-service website terms for a
        {SITE.serviceNoun} business.
      </p>

      <h2>1. Who We Are</h2>
      <p>
        {SITE.name} ({SITE.legalName}) provides residential and commercial {SITE.serviceNoun} work in and around {SITE.city} and {SITE.region}.
        We are a locally owned business.
      </p>

      <h2>2. Use of This Website</h2>
      <p>You agree to use this website only for lawful purposes and to:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Provide accurate information when submitting forms</li>
        <li>Not attempt to disrupt, scrape, or misuse the site or its systems</li>
        <li>Not submit harmful code, spam, or misleading project requests</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        We may suspend or limit access to the site if we believe these terms are being violated.
      </p>

      <h2>3. Estimate &amp; Appointment Requests</h2>
      <p>
        Submitting a form or booking a service visit does
        <strong>not</strong> create a binding service contract. Estimates, pricing,
        timelines, and scope are informational
        until confirmed in writing after an on-site diagnosis.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Final pricing may change based on material selections, structural findings, permit requirements, and scope adjustments</li>
        <li>Scheduling depends on crew availability, material lead times, and weather</li>
        <li>Financing is subject to third-party lender approval and separate terms</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>4. Services &amp; Workmanship</h2>
      <p>
        Actual work is governed by the written proposal, work authorization, invoices, and
        any warranty documents you receive. Unless otherwise stated in writing:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>We perform work in a professional manner consistent with industry standards</li>
        <li>Manufacturer warranties apply according to product terms; workmanship warranty details are provided at contract</li>
        <li>Weather, material lead times, and HOA or permit requirements may affect scheduling</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>5. Payments</h2>
      <p>
        Payment terms are specified in your written agreement. Deposits, progress payments, or final
        balances may be required. Unpaid balances may result in delayed scheduling, collection
        activity, or lien rights as allowed by applicable {SITE.state} law.
      </p>

      <h2>6. SMS &amp; Marketing Communications</h2>
      <p>
        If you opt in, {SITE.name} may send project updates and, where consented, marketing texts or
        emails. Message frequency varies. Message and data rates may apply. Reply <strong>STOP</strong>
        to cancel SMS; reply <strong>HELP</strong> for help. Consent is not required to receive an
        estimate.
      </p>

      <h2>7. Intellectual Property</h2>
      <p>
        Site content — including text, branding, logos, photographs, and layout — is owned by or
        licensed to {SITE.name}. You may not copy, republish, or commercially reuse site materials
        without our prior written permission, except for personal, non-commercial viewing.
      </p>

      <h2>8. Third-Party Services</h2>
      <p>
        The site may integrate maps, analytics, financing tools, or other third-party services. We
        are not responsible for third-party content, availability, or policies. Your use of those
        services may be subject to additional terms.
      </p>

      <h2>9. Disclaimers</h2>
      <p>
        The website and demo content are provided “as is.” To the fullest extent permitted by law, we
        disclaim warranties of merchantability, fitness for a particular purpose, and non-infringement
        regarding website content. Online examples of pricing, reviews, team bios, and project photos
        may be illustrative for this demo environment.
      </p>

      <h2>10. Limitation of Liability</h2>
      <p>
        To the fullest extent permitted by law, {SITE.name} and its owners, employees, and agents are
        not liable for indirect, incidental, special, consequential, or punitive damages arising from
        your use of the website. Our total liability related to website use shall not exceed one
        hundred dollars ($100), except where liability cannot be limited under {SITE.state} law. This
        section does not limit liability arising from a signed service agreement, which is
        governed by that agreement.
      </p>

      <h2>11. Indemnification</h2>
      <p>
        You agree to indemnify and hold harmless {SITE.name} from claims arising out of your misuse
        of the site, inaccurate form submissions, or violation of these terms, except to the extent
        caused by our willful misconduct.
      </p>

      <h2>12. Governing Law</h2>
      <p>
        These terms are governed by the laws of the State of {SITE.state}, without regard to conflict
        of law rules. Disputes related to website use shall be resolved in state or federal courts
        located in {SITE.city}, {SITE.state}, unless another venue is required by a signed service
        contract.
      </p>

      <h2>13. Changes</h2>
      <p>
        We may update these Terms of Service at any time. The “Last updated” date will reflect the
        latest revision. Continued use of the site after changes means you accept the updated terms.
      </p>

      <h2>14. Contact</h2>
      <p>Questions about these Terms of Service:</p>
      <p>
        <strong>{SITE.name}</strong><br />
        {address}<br />
        Email: <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a><br />
        Phone: <a href={telHref}>{SITE.phone}</a><br />
        License: {SITE.license}
      </p>
    </div>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .legal-page {
    padding-top: 5.5rem;
    padding-bottom: 4rem;
    background: var(--panel);
  }

  .legal-content {
    padding: clamp(1.75rem, 4vw, 2.75rem);
    max-width: 860px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    background: #fff;
  }

  .legal-content h1 {
    font-size: clamp(2.5rem, 6vw, 3.5rem);
    line-height: 0.95;
    margin-bottom: 0.6rem;
    color: var(--deep);
  }

  .legal-updated {
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--muted);
    margin-bottom: 1.25rem;
  }

  .legal-content h2 {
    margin: 1.75rem 0 0.55rem;
    color: var(--deep);
    font-family: var(--font-body);
    font-size: 1.2rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    line-height: 1.3;
  }

  .legal-content p,
  .legal-content li {
    color: var(--muted);
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .legal-content ul {
    margin: 0.5rem 0 1rem;
    padding-left: 1.25rem;
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.4rem;
  }

  .legal-content a {
    font-weight: 600;
  }
</style>
